{"term":"pack up","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:64b9a5be76758baecf","definition":"To give in; to give up; to leave in defeat.","example":"Our last batter just struck out. Time to pack it up, boys.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1663fc9cb2c321ce08","definition":"To clear away and place into storage.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:91d01392603ad5ff7c","definition":"To put back together.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:13ffb552a1467ee089","definition":"To move one’s residence.","example":"After 5 months in Madrid, I've decided it is time to pack up.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8507644007487db39a","definition":"To prepare for shipping, as a gift.","example":"Pack up the crates.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1622214fadb8885a5","definition":"To put into bags to prepare to move.","example":"Julie DeLongpre: Is there anything I can do to help?\nAllen Gregory DeLongpre: Well, I guess maybe you could pack up your belongings-\nJulie: All right.\nAnd go back to wherever the hell you came from. Does that make sense? So, it does make sense? No?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ffc00f8eb4c41a2ae3","definition":"To break, to cease to function.","example":"The shop was driven by a hiccoughy old gas engine which sometimes packed up, to the great delight of all the juveniles.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:86dd4667521983f663","definition":"To fill a pipe with cannabis for smoking.","example":"Ralph, it's your turn to pack up the bowl.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{},"wordFamily":[]}